  "question": {
    "text": "Two planets <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of equal mass are having their period of revolutions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>. These planets are revolving in the circular orbits of radii <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math> respectively. Which out of the following would be the correct relationship of their orbits?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>-</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From&nbsp;Kepler&#39;s law of periods,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></math></p>"
  }
}